7	2	82	\N	Our role	our-role	0	2016-07-01 04:15:00.082835	2016-08-01 04:58:05.480849	GeneralContent	\N	published	97cad92d-7e84-4ad5-92b6-3acdae0216cc	\N	\N	{"name": "Our role", "options": {"toc": 1}, "content_body": "## What we do\\r\\n\\r\\nWe help the communications sector stay competitive and innovative by providing advice, delivering programs and conducting research.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe also manage programs that encourage artists, support Australia's cultural heritage and help the public to experience arts and culture.\\r\\n\\r\\nOur priorities include advising the government on:\\r\\n\\r\\n* The opportunities being created by changes in digital technology.\\r\\n* How to deliver digital infrastructure (such as the nbn) to help grow the economy.\\r\\n* How to promote competition in the communications markets and make sure all Australians can access basic services while being protected from inappropriate content.\\r\\n* How to give all Australians access to artistic and cultural activities, performances and exhibitions.\\r\\n* How to support Australia's arts and cultural sectors through research, funding, training and programs. \\r\\n\\r\\n[Read more about what we do](#)\\r\\n\\r\\n## Information and services\\r\\n\\r\\nWe provide information and deliver services related to communications and the arts.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Internet\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Internet gambling](#)**  \\r\\nInformation about online gambling.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Internet governance](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on the laws and rules that apply to the internet.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Spam](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on how to reduce internet spam.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Broadband](#)**  \\r\\nInformation about the nbn and internet service providers.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Online safety](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on cyber security and staying safe online.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Television\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Television (TV) reception](/television-tv-reception)**  \\r\\nInformation on improving television reception.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Television (TV) and radio services](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on television and radio services.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Phone\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Phone](#)**  \\r\\nInformation about landline, mobile and satellite phone services.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Radio\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Radio and television (TV) services](#)**  \\r\\nInformation about radio and television (TV) services.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Radio and television (TV) content rules](#)**  \\r\\nInformation about media complaints and laws.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Post\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Postal services](#)**  \\r\\nInformation about postal services.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Spectrum\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Spectrum](#)**  \\r\\nInformation about the electromagnetic spectrum.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Copyright\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Intellectual property (IP)](#)**  \\r\\nInformation about protecting and registering intellectual property.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Classification\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Classification](#)**  \\r\\nInformation about media ratings.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Arts\\r\\n\\r\\n**[The Arts](#)**  \\r\\nInformation about the arts including funding.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Media ownership\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Media ownership laws](#)**  \\r\\nInformation about media ownership laws.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Portfolio agencies we work with\\r\\n\\r\\nA portolio is an area of responsibility for how Australia is run. Our Department is part of the Communications portfolio, which is led by the [Minister for Communications](https://gov-au-beta.apps.platform.digital.gov.au/minister-for-communications).\\r\\n\\r\\nWe work closely with the other government agencies within our portfolio:\\r\\n\\r\\n* **[Australia Council for the Arts](http://www.australiacouncil.gov.au/)**   \\r\\nThe Australian Government's arts funding and advisory body.\\r\\n* **[Australia Post](http://auspost.com.au/)**  \\r\\nProviding reliable and affordable postal, retail, financial and travel services.\\r\\n* **[Australian Broadcasting corporation (ABC)](http://www.abc.net.au/)**  \\r\\nAustralia’s public broadcaster, including national and local television and radio programs.\\r\\n* **[Australian Communications and Media Authority (ACMA)](http://www.acma.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nResponsible for the regulation of broadcasting, the internet, radiocommunications and telecommunications.\\r\\n* **[Australian Film Television and Radio School (AFTRS)](https://www.aftrs.edu.au/)**  \\r\\nThe leading institution for the education and training of creative talent.\\r\\n* **[Australian National Maritime Museum](http://www.anmm.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nAustralia’s national centre for maritime collections, exhibitions, research and archaeology.\\r\\n* **[Bundanon Trust](https://bundanon.com.au/)**  \\r\\nSupporting arts practice and engagement through education, exhibition and performance programs.\\r\\n* **[Australia Business Arts Foundation (operating as Creative Partnerships Australia)](https://www.creativepartnershipsaustralia.org.au/)**  \\r\\nBringing artists, donors, businesses and arts organisations together to promote a more sustainable and vibrant arts sector.\\r\\n* **[The Museum of Australian Democracy](http://moadoph.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nHelping people to understand Australia’s social and political history by interpreting the past and present and exploring the future.\\r\\n* **[National Film and Sound Archive](http://www.nfsa.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nThe nation’s living archive – collecting, preserving and sharing our rich audiovisual heritage.\\r\\n* **[National Gallery of Australia (NGA)](http://nga.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nAustralia's national cultural institution for the visual arts.\\r\\n* **[National Library of Australia (NLA)](https://www.nla.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nEnsuring that important documentary resources are collected, preserved and made accessible to the public.\\r\\n* **[National Museum of Australia](http://www.nma.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nA social history museum exploring the land, nation and people of Australia.\\r\\n* **[National Portrait Gallery Australia (NPGA)](http://www.portrait.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nThe national collection of portraits of Australians reflects the breadth and energy of Australian culture and endeavour.\\r\\n* **[NBN Co Limited](http://www.nbnco.com.au/)**  \\r\\nDelivering Australia’s first national, open access broadband network to all Australians.\\r\\n* **[Office of the Children’s e-Safety Commissioner](https://www.esafety.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nCommitted to helping young people have safe, positive experiences online.\\r\\n* **[Screen Australia](http://www.screenaustralia.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nFunding the production of everything from feature films to documentaries, television drama, children’s programs and online web series.\\r\\n* **[Special broadcasting service (SBS)](http://www.sbs.com.au/)**  \\r\\nAustralia’s multicultural and multilingual broadcaster.", "short_summary": "Through our advice and programs we aim to make communication technologies and the arts better for all Australians."}	2016-08-01 04:58:05.47769
16	2	82	\N	Careers	careers	3	2016-07-04 23:03:24.763132	2016-08-02 02:05:44.571717	GeneralContent	\N	published	a183986f-5191-46d4-8cc8-d8bf30ab055b	\N	\N	{"name": "Careers", "options": {"toc": 1}, "content_body": "## What we work on\\r\\n\\r\\nWe promote an innovative and competitive communications sector by undertaking analysis, providing advice and delivering programs.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe also manage programs that encourage excellence in art, support for cultural heritage and public access to arts and culture.\\r\\n\\r\\n[Learn more about our role](/department-of-communications-and-the-arts/our-role).\\r\\n\\r\\n## Jobs\\r\\n\\r\\n### [Current job vacancies](https://communications.nga.net.au)\\r\\nSee what roles we have available now.\\r\\n\\r\\n### [Graduate Program](#)\\r\\nGraduate employment opportunities are usually advertised between February and June.\\r\\n\\r\\n## The benefits of working here\\r\\n\\r\\nWorking with us can give you a rewarding and exciting career. \\r\\n\\r\\nFor more details on any of the items below, please see our [Enterprise agreement information](#).\\r\\n\\r\\n### Location\\r\\n\\r\\nWe are centrally located in Canberra, with offices around the country.\\r\\n\\r\\nA range of on-site facilities help staff to balance their work and personal needs including:\\r\\n\\r\\n* Carers' rooms.\\r\\n* Access to new technology to support flexible work arrangements including laptops, Wi-Fi and remote network access\\r\\n\\r\\n### Competitive remuneration package\\r\\n\\r\\nWe offer a good salary, generous leave conditions, vacation care and an attractive superannuation scheme.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Flexible working arrangements\\r\\n\\r\\nWe provide access to new technology to support flexible work arrangements (such as the ability to work off-site) as well as flexible working hours.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Wellbeing Program and social club\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Wellbeing Program includes seminars and activities that focus on the social, mental and physical health of employees. It includes:\\r\\n\\r\\n* free influenza vaccinations\\r\\n* a carer's room\\r\\n* health seminars\\r\\n* quit smoking assistance\\r\\n* annual health checks\\r\\n* cooking demonstrations\\r\\n* physical activities such as lunchtime walking groups\\r\\n\\r\\n### Learning and development\\r\\n\\r\\nOur employees have opportunities for learning and development throughout their careers including:\\r\\n\\r\\n* an induction program for new employees\\r\\n* a core training program with short courses for business skills and knowledge\\r\\n* in-house capability development programs\\r\\n* development programs to build management and leadership skills\\r\\n* a staff job rotation program and portfolio agency secondment program to help our employees broaden their skills and knowledge\\r\\n* access to mentoring programs\\r\\n\\r\\n### Study assistance\\r\\n\\r\\nStudybank is our study assistance program. It helps our employees develop their work-related skills through access to:\\r\\n\\r\\n* up to 75 hours paid leave per semester for study\\r\\n* financial assistance of up to $5000 per calendar year as per the Enterprise Agreement.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Employee Assistance Program (EAP)\\r\\n\\r\\nThe EAP is a confidential, professional short-term counselling service. It is a free service for our employees and their immediate families.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Smoke-free workplace\\r\\n\\r\\nAs an employer, we have a duty of care to protect our staff from passive smoking while they are working. We provide financial assistance to staff and members of their immediate families who want to quit smoking. There are designated smoking areas.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Support for carers\\r\\n\\r\\nWe offer services to support carers including:\\r\\n\\r\\n* The Vacation Childcare Subsidisation Program – for children aged between five and 12 years. To qualify, children must attend a registered child care service during the school holidays.\\r\\n* Carers’ room – available for staff who need to take care of immediate family members in an emergency. It gives people an alternative to using leave. Conditions of use apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Eldercare\\r\\n\\r\\nOur eldercare information kit contains information on eldercare issues and how to deal with them. The kit is a national resource that has information on all states and territories.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Employment agreement information\\r\\n\\r\\nOur enterprise agreement sets the terms and conditions for our employees:\\r\\n\\r\\n* [Department of Communications Enterprise Agreement 2015-18](#)\\r\\n* [Enterprise agreement pay scale](#)\\r\\n* [Enterprise Agreement s24(1) determination](#)\\r\\n\\r\\n## How to apply\\r\\n\\r\\nVisit our [How to apply](#) page to learn more about:\\r\\n\\r\\n* how to prepare your application\\r\\n* our engagement conditions\\r\\n* the selection process", "short_summary": "Information on current vacancies, the benefits of working at our department and how to apply for a job."}	2016-08-02 02:05:44.56277
