54	7	86	\N	Careers	careers	3	2016-07-06 01:05:25.946613	2016-07-29 05:48:26.453746	GeneralContent	\N	published	4a29143a-06bf-41bd-bc17-a7fcb71b785e	\N	\N	{"name": "Careers", "options": {"toc": 1, "suppress_in_nav": false}, "content_body": "## What we work on\\r\\n\\r\\nWe provide fresh thinking and sound advice to the Government on economic, domestic and international issues.\\r\\n\\r\\n[Learn more about our role](/department-of-the-prime-minister-and-cabinet/our-role).\\r\\n\\r\\n## Job opportunities\\r\\n\\r\\n### [Current job opportunities](http://dpmc.nga.net.au/cp/)\\r\\nSee what roles we have available now.\\r\\n\\r\\n### [Graduate Program](#)\\r\\nGraduate employment opportunities are usually advertised between February and June.\\r\\n\\r\\n## The benefits of working here\\r\\n\\r\\nWe offer exciting and fulfilling work at the heart of government with career development and networking opportunities difficult to find elsewhere.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe also offer the opportunity to work with strong, smart, visionary and experienced leaders who encourage and support you to develop your interests and expertise and achieve your ambitions.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor more details on any of the items below, please see our [Enterprise agreement](#).\\r\\n\\r\\n### Locations\\r\\n\\r\\nOur National Office is located in Canberra (Barton and Woden). We also have offices in every capital city and in regional and remote locations.\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom time to time you may also have the opportunity to work from other locations around the country and the globe.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Competitive remuneration package\\r\\n\\r\\nWe offer a good salary, generous leave conditions and an attractive superannuation scheme.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Flexible working arrangements\\r\\n\\r\\nWe support flexible work arrangements (such as the ability to work off-site) as well as flexible working hours.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Wellbeing program\\r\\n\\r\\nOur employees are encouraged to maintain healthy and active lifestyles. To support this, we provide:\\r\\n\\r\\n* The Employee Assistance Program (EAP) – a confidential, professional short-term counselling service. It is a free service for our employees and their immediate families.\\r\\n* A program of health activities. Employees are encouraged to participate. \\r\\n\\r\\n### Learning and development\\r\\n\\r\\nWe actively support learning and development opportunities for our employees including:\\r\\n\\r\\n* on the job learning opportunities including special projects, taskforces and secondments\\r\\n* core skill training such as writing skills, Microsoft office suite, project management and CABNET\\r\\n* strategic skill sets including policy and legislative processes and developing business cases\\r\\n* seminar series\\r\\n* a mentoring program\\r\\n* the development of case studies\\r\\n\\r\\n### Study assistance\\r\\n\\r\\nWe may provide assistance for employees undertaking tertiary education relevant to our operational needs including:\\r\\n\\r\\n* financial assistance\\r\\n* study leave\\r\\n* access to flexible working arrangements for study purposes\\r\\n\\r\\n### Support for carers\\r\\n\\r\\nWe offer services to support for carers including:\\r\\n\\r\\n* A family assistance information service that can provide information on care services such as child care centres, vacation care, hostels, home care services and nursing homes. \\r\\n* Our carers’ room is available for staff who need to take care of immediate family members in an emergency. It gives people an alternative to using leave.\\r\\n* Payment for certain costs associated with the care of a family member or dependent where an employee is required to travel or work outside their normal hours.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Diversity and Inclusion\\r\\n\\r\\nWe are committed to supporting workplace diversity and aim to create an environment that values people with different backgrounds, experiences and perspectives.​​\\r\\n\\r\\nWe provide a sensitive and supportive environment for Indigenous people and support Australian Government programs in relation to the employment of Indigenous people.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe also committed to increasing employment opportunities and accessibility for people with disability. \\r\\n\\r\\n## Employment agreement information\\r\\n\\r\\nOur enterprise agreement sets the terms and conditions for our employees:\\r\\n\\r\\n* [Department of Prime Minister and the Cabinet Enterprise Agreement 2011-14](#)\\r\\n\\r\\n## How to apply\\r\\n\\r\\nVisit our [How to apply page](#) to learn more about:\\r\\n\\r\\n* how to prepare your application,\\r\\n* our engagement conditions,\\r\\n* the selection process and more.", "short_summary": "Information on current vacancies, the benefits of working here and how to apply for job opportunities."}	2016-07-29 05:48:26.450653
