45	8	87	\N	Careers	careers	3	2016-07-06 01:01:49.790571	2016-08-02 02:05:26.220496	GeneralContent	\N	published	e505245d-670d-4bae-8ecb-23bcb557285a	\N	\N	{"name": "Careers", "options": {"toc": 1, "suppress_in_nav": false}, "content_body": "## What we work on\\r\\n\\r\\nOur department is a trusted adviser to the Australian Government on financial and business issues.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe manage the Budget and financial reporting processes and work with organisations to make sure the government has the information it needs to make important decisions.\\r\\n\\r\\n[Learn more about our role](/department-of-finance/our-role).\\r\\n\\r\\n## Jobs\\r\\n\\r\\n### [Current job vacancies](https://financejobs.nga.net.au/cp/)\\r\\nSee what roles we have available now.\\r\\n\\r\\n### [Graduate Program](#)\\r\\nGraduate employment opportunities are usually advertised between February and June.\\r\\n\\r\\n### [Career Starter Program](#)\\r\\nDon’t know what to do when you finish Year 12? Working in government can take you places.\\r\\n\\r\\n### [Driving Opportunities at COMCAR](#)\\r\\nWork as a casual driver across Australia and help provide transport for VIP clients, visiting dignitaries and at major events.\\r\\n\\r\\n## The benefits of working here\\r\\n\\r\\nJoining the Department of Finance is a great way to make your mark, build professional skills and contribute to key Australian Government priorities.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor more details on any of the items below, please see our [Enterprise agreement](#).\\r\\n\\r\\n### Location and facilities\\r\\n\\r\\nWe are centrally located in Canberra, with offices around the country.\\r\\n\\r\\nA range of on-site facilities help staff to balance their work and personal needs including: \\r\\n\\r\\n* Childcare facilities\\r\\n* A library\\r\\n* Carers' and Mothers' rooms\\r\\n* Health and fitness facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Competitive remuneration package\\r\\n\\r\\nWe provide competitive salaries with annual increases, generous leave conditions (including carers' leave) and an attractive superannuation scheme.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Flexible working arrangements\\r\\n\\r\\nWe support flexible work arrangements including flex-time, part-time work and working from home.\\r\\n\\r\\n### A supportive workplace\\r\\n\\r\\nOur employees are encouraged to maintain healthy and active lifestyles. To support this, we provide:\\r\\n\\r\\n* Social Club – conducts a range of regular activities during the year including charity fundraising events, lunchtime sport and the premier social event, the Finance Ball.\\r\\n* The Employee Assistance Program (EAP) – a confidential, professional short-term counselling service. It is a free service for our employees and their immediate families.\\r\\n* A [Support for Breastfeeding at Work Policy](#).\\r\\n* Community service (emergency management and jury service) leave.\\r\\n* Financial reimbursement for professional memberships relevant to our operational needs.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Staff networks\\r\\n\\r\\n* Staff Consultative Group (SCG) – provides advice to management on workplace issues and feedback to employees regarding employment matters.\\r\\n* Women’s Network – acts as an agent of cultural change and continuous improvement within the Department.\\r\\n* Finance's Professional Community of Accountants – provides regular updates on the latest in the accounting environment, within Australia and internationally.\\r\\n* Executive Assistant’s Network (EA Network) – shares information and ideas and to keep up-to-date with new policies, procedures, and technology.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### Learning and development\\r\\n\\r\\nWe actively support learning and development opportunities for our employees including:\\r\\n\\r\\n* leadership programs\\r\\n* coaching and mentoring\\r\\n* professional skills training\\r\\n* Learning Centre presentations from high-profile external speakers\\r\\n* seminars presented by internal subject matter experts\\r\\n* on the job learning opportunities\\r\\n\\r\\nWe are also accredited as a CPA (Certified Practicing Accountant) Australia Recognised Employer to the Knowledge Level. \\r\\n\\r\\n### Study assistance\\r\\n\\r\\nWe may provide assistance for employees undertaking tertiary education relevant to our operational needs including:\\r\\n\\r\\n* financial assistance\\r\\n* study leave\\r\\n* access to flexible working arrangements for study purposes\\r\\n\\r\\n### Diversity and Inclusion\\r\\n\\r\\nWe are an inclusive organisation in which different skills, perspectives and backgrounds are valued. \\r\\n                  \\r\\nWe aim to increase representation and support for the following diversity groups:\\r\\n\\r\\n* Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples\\r\\n* people with disability\\r\\n* women in senior management\\r\\n\\r\\nOur workplace plans and programs include:\\r\\n\\r\\n* [Diversity Strategy 2013-2015](#)\\r\\n* [Diversity Action Plan 2013-2015](#)\\r\\n* [Reconciliation Action Plan 2013-2015](#)\\r\\n\\r\\n## Employment agreement information\\r\\n\\r\\nOur enterprise agreement sets the terms and conditions for our employees:\\r\\n\\r\\n* [Department of Finance Enterprise Agreement 2015-2018](#)\\r\\n\\r\\n## How to apply\\r\\n\\r\\nVisit our [How to apply page](#) to learn more about:\\r\\n\\r\\n* how to prepare your application\\r\\n* our engagement conditions\\r\\n* the selection process", "short_summary": "Information on current vacancies, the benefits of working here and how to apply for job opportunities."}	2016-08-02 02:05:26.217408
