24	5	84	\N	Our responsibilities	our-role	0	2016-07-06 00:54:10.416392	2016-08-02 02:09:00.60336	GeneralContent	\N	published	a311e5fe-9e6f-4903-8f6c-b6bbd53dcb7f	\N	\N	{"name": "Our role", "options": {"toc": 1, "suppress_in_nav": false}, "content_body": "## What we do\\r\\n\\r\\nWe direct Australia’s health and aged care systems, as well as sporting programs.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have a variety of responsibilities but one common goal: better health and wellbeing for all Australians, now and for future generations.\\r\\n\\r\\nOur focus is on:\\r\\n\\r\\n* providing evidence-based advice on health issues\\r\\n* improving health programs, research and laws\\r\\n* working closely with consumers, health organisations and other government agencies\\r\\n\\r\\n[Read more about what we do](#)\\r\\n\\r\\n## Information and services\\r\\n\\r\\nWe provide information and deliver services related to health, aged care and sport.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Health services\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Immunisation](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on how to immunise you and your family against diseases.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Public toilet map](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on how to find the nearest public toilet.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[My Health Record](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on how to manage a secure online summary of your health information.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Ageing and aged care](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on how to get support services for older Australians.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Diseases and conditions\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Diseases and conditions](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on various health conditions and issues.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Hearing](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on reducing the impact of hearing loss.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Palliative care](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on how to improve quality of life for people with life-threatening illnesses.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Mental health](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on improving mental health.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Health emergencies](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on bioterrorism, natural disasters, disease outbreaks and more.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Healthy eating and drinking\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Alcohol](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on reducing the dangers of alcohol.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Healthy living](#)**  \\r\\nInformation health eating, exercise and lifestyle.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Healthy workplaces](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on keeping workplaces safe.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Food standards and safety](#)**  \\r\\nInformation to help reduce any risks related to food.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Smoking and tobacco](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on reducing the risks of tobacco.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Drugs](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on preventing harmful drug use.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Health insurance\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Private health insurance](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on private insurance for hospital visits and general treatments.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Health industry management\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Health workforce](#)**  \\r\\nInformation to improve the quality of Australia's health workforce.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Sport\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Sports](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on the government sporting programs.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Sports anti-doping](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on reducing cheating in sport.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Sports fundraising](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on how to raise funds for sporting activities.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Portfolio agencies we work with\\r\\n\\r\\nA portfolio is an area of responsibility for how Australia is run. Our department is part of the Health and Aged Care portfolio, which is led by the [Minister for Health](/minister-for-health).\\r\\n\\r\\nWe work closely with the other government agencies within our portfolio:\\r\\n\\r\\n* **[Australian Commission on Safety and Quality in Health Care (ACSQHC)](http://www.safetyandquality.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nLeading and coordinating improvements in health care safety and quality.\\r\\n* **[Australian Institute of Health and Welfare (AIHW)](http://www.aihw.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nProviding information and statistics on Australia’s health and welfare.\\r\\n* **[Australian Organ and Tissue Donation and Transplantation Authority (AOTDTA)](http://www.donatelife.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nDelivering Australia's national reform program to achieve increases in organ donation and transplantation.\\r\\n* **[Australian Radiation Protection and Nuclear Safety Agency (ARPANSA)](http://www.arpansa.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nProtecting people and the environment from the harmful effect of radiation.\\r\\n* **[Australian Sports Anti-Doping Authority (ASADA)](https://www.asada.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nWorking to make all sports free from performance-enhancing drugs.\\r\\n* **[Australian Sports Commission (ASC)](http://www.ausport.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nProviding leadership and support for the sport industry, with the goal of getting more Australians participating and excelling in sport.\\r\\n* **[Australian Sports Foundation (ASF)](http://www.asf.org.au/)**  \\r\\nDedicated to raising money for sport in Australia and providing an easy-to-use platform to help with fundraising.\\r\\n* **[Cancer Australia (CA)](https://canceraustralia.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nWorking to reduce the impact of cancer on all Australians. \\r\\n* **[Food Standards Australia New Zealand (FSANZ)](http://www.foodstandards.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nManaging the Australia New Zealand Food Standards Code, which lists requirements for foods such as additives, safety and labelling.\\r\\n* **[National Blood Authority (NBA)](https://www.blood.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nSaving and improving Australian lives through a world-class blood supply.\\r\\n* **[National Health and Medical Research Council (NHMRC)](https://www.nhmrc.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nSupporting health and medical research and providing advice for all Australians.\\r\\n* **[National Health Funding Body (NHFB)](http://www.nhfb.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nSupporting public hospitals to make their funding reports more transparent and efficient.\\r\\n* **[Independent Hospital Pricing Authority (IHPA)](https://www.ihpa.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nImproving Australian public hospitals through a new way of funding that increases efficiency and transparency.\\r\\n* **[Professional Services Review (PSR)](http://www.psr.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nProtecting patients and the community from the risks of unacceptable behaviour by health professionals.\\r\\n* **[National Health Performance Authority (NHPA)](http://www.nhpa.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nMonitoring the performance of hospitals and other organisations that provide health care services.\\r\\n* **[National Mental Health Commission (NMHC)](http://www.mentalhealthcommission.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nProviding reports and advice to the community and government on what’s working and what’s not with mental health services.\\r\\n* **[Gene Technology Regulator (GTR)](http://www.ogtr.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nProtecting the health and safety of people and the environment by identifying the risks of gene technology.\\r\\n* **[Director, National Industrial Chemicals Notification and Assessment Scheme (NICNAS)](https://www.nicnas.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nAssessing the risks of industrial chemicals and providing information on how to use them safely.", "short_summary": "We give advice, create programs and regulate services to provide a better standard of living for all Australians."}	2016-08-02 02:09:00.600045
