27	5	84	\N	Careers	careers	3	2016-07-06 00:55:14.233877	2016-07-29 05:52:12.11719	GeneralContent	\N	published	05d1436c-4f85-490c-afbc-89d7f709651e	\N	\N	{"name": "Careers", "options": {"toc": 1, "suppress_in_nav": false}, "content_body": "## What we work on\\r\\n\\r\\nWe direct Australia’s health and aged care system, as well as sporting programs.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have a variety of responsibilities but one common goal: better health and wellbeing for all Australians, now and for future generations.\\r\\n\\r\\n[Learn more about our role](/department-of-health/our-role).\\r\\n\\r\\n## Job opportunities\\r\\n\\r\\n### [Current job opportunities](http://healthjobs.nga.net.au/cp/index.cfm)\\r\\nSee what roles we have available now.\\r\\n\\r\\n### [Graduate Program](#)\\r\\nGraduate employment opportunities are usually advertised between February and June.\\r\\n\\r\\n### [Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Entry-Level Programs](#)\\r\\nWe participate in the APSC Indigenous Pathways Program and the Department of Employment’s Indigenous Australian Government Development Program.\\r\\n\\r\\n## The benefits of working here\\r\\n\\r\\nFor more details on any of the items below, please see our [Enterprise agreement](#).\\r\\n\\r\\n### Locations\\r\\n\\r\\nWe are centrally located in Canberra, with offices around the country.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Competitive remuneration package\\r\\n\\r\\nWe offer a good salary, generous leave conditions (including carer’s leave) and an attractive superannuation scheme.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Flexible working arrangements\\r\\n\\r\\nWe support arrangements for flexible work conditions including:\\r\\n\\r\\n* Access to flextime and time-in-lieu arrangements upon negotiation with manager.\\r\\n* Flexible arrangements for staff with family responsibilities, including carer’s leave.\\r\\n* Negotiable part time working hours.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Healthy workplace\\r\\n\\r\\nOur employees are encouraged to maintain healthy and active lifestyles. To support this, we provide:\\r\\n\\r\\n* The Employee Assistance Program (EAP) – a confidential, professional short-term counselling service. It is a free service for our employees and their immediate families.\\r\\n* Influenza vaccinations for all interested staff.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Learning and development\\r\\n\\r\\nWe believe in developing employee work skills and experiences. Staff are provided with support, opportunities and assistance to learn through:\\r\\n\\r\\n* Internal on-the-job and off-the-job training programs.\\r\\n* Accredited courses for required roles.\\r\\n* eLearning and online learning resources.\\r\\n* Individual development plans that focus on capability needs.\\r\\n* Department (tertiary) study schemes and professional development support.\\r\\n* Learning programs that partner with professional educational institutions and academic bodies\\r\\nprogrammes to recognise and grow talent.\\r\\n* Studybank - in some cases we may provide leave to undertake tertiary and other vocational education courses.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Diversity and equality\\r\\n\\r\\nWe aim to be a model employer, providing an inclusive workplace that is understanding and respectful of differences such as gender, race, disability or age. Our workplace plans and programs include:\\r\\n\\r\\n* [Workforce Diversity Programme 2013-2016](#)\\r\\n* [Reconciliation Action Plan](#)\\r\\n* [Disability Workforce Action Plan](#)\\r\\n* [Agency Multicultural Plan](#)\\r\\n\\r\\nWe are also members of [Pride in Diversity](http://www.prideindiversity.com.au/) and gold members of the  [Australian Network on Disability](http://www.and.org.au/).\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have appointed senior members of staff to the roles of Diversity Champion and Disability Champion to progress action on diversity issues. \\r\\n\\r\\nAs a further commitment to workplace diversity, we have also established the National Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Staff Network, Staff with Disability Network and Health Pride Network.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Employment agreement information\\r\\n\\r\\nOur enterprise agreement sets the terms and conditions for our employees:\\r\\n\\r\\n* [Department of Health Enterprise Agreement 2016-2019](#)\\r\\n\\r\\n## How to apply\\r\\n\\r\\nVisit our [How to apply page](#) to learn more about:\\r\\n\\r\\n* how to prepare your application,\\r\\n* our engagement conditions,\\r\\n* the selection process and more.", "short_summary": "Information on current vacancies, the benefits of working here and how to apply for job opportunities."}	2016-07-29 05:52:12.114364
