51	7	86	\N	Our responsibilities	our-role	0	2016-07-06 01:04:39.47743	2016-08-01 04:37:43.449713	GeneralContent	\N	published	5089190d-2bcc-40eb-9473-7d13b320dca4	\N	\N	{"name": "Our role", "options": {"toc": 1, "suppress_in_nav": false}, "content_body": "## What we do\\r\\n\\r\\nOur focus, put simply, is to find new ways to improve the lives of all Australians.\\r\\n\\r\\nIt’s our responsibility to stay informed on the many issues facing Australia and consider the opinions of people from across government, business, the not-for-profit sector and the community.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis lets us provide clear advice to the [Prime Minister, the Cabinet, Portfolio Ministers and Assistant Ministers](/department-of-the-prime-minister-and-cabinet/people-and-structure).\\r\\n\\r\\nOur priorities include:\\r\\n\\r\\n* Support the Prime Minister, as the head of the Australian Government, and the activities of the Cabinet.\\r\\n* Work with different government agencies to develop policies and decisions based on a whole-of-government approach.\\r\\n* Provide advice on the Government’s domestic and foreign policies with a focus on practical changes to improve the lives of all Australians.\\r\\n* Supervise national security matters and manage national taskforces.\\r\\n* Work across a variety of portfolios to improve the lives of Indigenous Australians.\\r\\n* Promote gender equality, including in government operations and policy development.\\r\\n* Work with the Australian Public Service Commission to create a productive public sector.\\r\\n\\r\\n[Read more about what we do](#)\\r\\n\\r\\n## Information and services\\r\\n\\r\\nWe provide information and deliver services on issues including:\\r\\n\\r\\n* **[Cyber security](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on the Government’s strategies to reduce cybercrime and online threats.\\r\\n\\r\\n* **[Indigenous affairs](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on Government policies and programs for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people.\\r\\n\\r\\n* **[National security](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on national security and preventing terrorism.\\r\\n\\r\\n* **[Gender equality](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on women’s rights, gender discrimination laws and the Australian Government’s policies and programs.\\r\\n\\r\\n* **[Public data ](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on finding, accessing and reusing public information.\\r\\n\\r\\n* **[Climate change](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on how Australia is meeting climate change targets, improving the environment and supporting international responses.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Portfolio agencies we work with\\r\\n\\r\\nA portfolio is an area of responsibility for how Australia is run. Our department is part of the Prime Minister and Cabinet portfolio, which is led by the [Prime Minister](/prime-minister).\\r\\n\\r\\nWe work closely with the other government agencies within our portfolio:\\r\\n\\r\\n* **[Aboriginal Hostels Limited (AHL)](www.ahl.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nDelivering accommodation and support services across a national network of hostels.\\r\\n* **[Aboriginal Land Commissioner](#)**  \\r\\nPerforming inquiries and providing reports into traditional land claims in the Northern Territory.\\r\\n* **[Anindilyakwa Land Council (ALC)](http://anindilyakwa.com.au/)**  \\r\\nRepresenting the Traditional Owners of the Groote Archipelago.\\r\\n* **[Australian National Audit Office (ANAO)](https://www.anao.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nProviding the Australian Parliament with independent assessments of Government administration and financial reporting.\\r\\n* **[Australian Public Service Commission (APSC)](http://www.apsc.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nEnsuring the APS provides the service the country needs.\\r\\n* **[Central Land Council (CLC)](http://www.clc.org.au/)**  \\r\\nProviding services for the benefit of Traditional Owners and other Aboriginal residents of the southern half of the Northern Territory.\\r\\n* **[Digital Transformation Office (DTO)](https://www.dto.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nWorking with Government, users and private sector partners to create public services that are simpler, clearer and faster.\\r\\n* **[Indigenous Business Australia (IBA)](http://www.iba.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nAssisting Indigenous Australians to buy their own homes, own their own businesses and invest in commercial ventures. \\r\\n* **[Indigenous Land Corporation (ILC)](http://www.ilc.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nAssisting Indigenous people to acquire and manage land so they can achieve economic, environmental, social and cultural benefits. \\r\\n* **[National Australia Day Council Limited (NADC)](http://www.australiaday.org.au/about-us/national-australia-day-council/)**  \\r\\nCoordinating the Australia Day celebrations across the nation and the Australian of the Year Awards. \\r\\n* **[Northern Land Council (NLC)](http://www.nlc.org.au/)**  \\r\\nAssisting Aboriginal peoples in the Top End of the Northern Territory to acquire and manage their traditional lands and seas.\\r\\n* **[Office of Township Leasing](http://www.otl.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nWorking with communities to manage township leases and provide real benefits to Aboriginal traditional owners.\\r\\n* **[Office of National Assessments (ONA)](https://www.ona.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nAnalysing the world, anticipating change and strengthening outcomes for Australia.\\r\\n* **[Office of the Commonwealth Ombudsman](http://www.ombudsman.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nInvestigating and resolving disputes between people and the Australian Government.\\r\\n* **[Office of the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security](https://www.igis.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nReviewing the activities of the six Australian intelligence agencies.\\r\\n* **[Office of the Official Secretary to the Governor-General](https://www.gg.gov.au/official-secretary-governor-general)**  \\r\\nSupporting the Governor-General to perform their range of duties.\\r\\n* **[Office of the Registrar of Indigenous Corporations](http://www.oric.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nSupporting and regulating corporations through advice and training.\\r\\n* **[Outback Stores Pty Ltd](http://outbackstores.com.au/)**  \\r\\nProviding retail services to remote stores on behalf of Indigenous communities. \\r\\n* **[Tiwi Land Council](http://www.tiwilandcouncil.com/)**  \\r\\nAssisting Tiwi Traditional Owners retain, manage and benefit from their land, sea and culture.\\r\\n* **[Torres Strait Regional Authority (TSRA)](http://www.tsra.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nStrengthening the economic, social and cultural development of the Torres Strait. \\r\\n* **[Wreck Bay Aboriginal Community Council](http://www.wbacc.gov.au/)**  \\r\\nProviding community services for its members as well as land holding and management.", "short_summary": "We provide fresh thinking and sound advice to the Prime Minister and Cabinet on economic, domestic and international issues."}	2016-08-01 04:37:43.44635
