42	8	87	\N	Our responsibilities	our-role	0	2016-07-06 01:01:09.412211	2016-08-02 01:49:30.831262	GeneralContent	\N	published	fa1313cd-30d3-47ba-b991-90df3f00374c	\N	\N	{"name": "Our role", "options": {"toc": 1}, "content_body": "## What we do\\r\\n\\r\\nOur department is a trusted adviser to the Australian Government on financial and business issues.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe manage the Budget and financial reporting processes and work with organisations to make sure the government has the information it needs to make important decisions.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe run programs and create frameworks (such as laws and processes) to encourage government agencies to innovate and perform efficiently. \\r\\n\\r\\nWe also play a key role in managing the government’s assets (including investment funds, buildings and lands) for the benefit of taxpayers.\\r\\n\\r\\n[Read more about what we do](#)\\r\\n\\r\\n## Information and services\\r\\n\\r\\nWe provide information and deliver services related to finance.\\r\\n\\r\\n### The Budget and financial reporting\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Budget](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on the Australian Government’s economic plan.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Government insurance and risk management](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on the Australian Government’s insurance funds and risk management strategies.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Government spending rules\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Super for Australian Government agencies](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on how government agencies pay superannuation to their employees.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Australian Government advertising](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on how the government spends money on advertising.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Australian Government procurement and travel](#)**  \\r\\nInformation about how the government makes purchases and pays for travel arrangements for its employees.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Parliamentary entitlements](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on financial and other benefits received by members of Parliament.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Government assets\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Australian Government investment funds](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on government investment funds such as the Future Fund, the Nation-building Funds, the DisabilityCare Australia Fund and the Medical Research Future Fund.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Australian Government fleet and property management](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on how the government manages its building, lands and vehicles.\\r\\n\\r\\n**[Australian Government (ICT) Information and Communications Technology](#)**  \\r\\nInformation on the government’s services and strategies for communications technology.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Portfolio agencies we work with\\r\\n\\r\\nA portfolio is an area of responsibility for how Australia is run. Our department is part of the Finance portfolio, which is led by the [Minister for Finance](/minister-for-finance).\\r\\n\\r\\nWe work closely with the other government agencies within our portfolio:\\r\\n\\r\\n* **[Australian Electoral Commission (AEC)](#)**  \\r\\nProviding an independent voting system for Australian Government elections and referendums. \\r\\n* **[ASC Pty Ltd](#)**  \\r\\nBuilding and maintaining Australia’s frontline naval ships and submarines.\\r\\n* **[Commonwealth Superannuation Corporation](#)**  \\r\\nMeeting the superannuation needs of Australian Government employees and members of the Australian Defence Forces.\\r\\n* **[Future Fund Management Agency](#)**  \\r\\nInvesting funds for the benefit of future generations of Australians.", "short_summary": "We provide advice, solutions and leadership to help the Australian Government meet its financial goals."}	2016-08-02 01:49:30.828535
77	11	91	\N	About the Prime Minister	about-the-prime-minister	1	2016-07-14 01:38:56.561722	2016-07-29 03:02:45.860804	GeneralContent	\N	published	215bb76a-c234-4652-8b0d-6d1d2039c4c9	\N	\N	{"name": "About the Prime Minister", "content_body": "![Hon Malcom Turnbull MP](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AusDTO/gov-au-images/master/ministers/malcom-turnbull-fb.jpg)\\r\\n\\r\\n## The Hon Malcolm Turnbull MP\\r\\n\\r\\nLiberal Party of Australia\\r\\n\\r\\n### Political career\\r\\n\\r\\nMr Turnbull was sworn in as the 29th Prime Minister of Australia on 15 September 2015.\\r\\n\\r\\nHe previously served as the Communications Minister from September 2013.\\r\\n\\r\\nMr Turnbull was Leader of the Opposition from 16 September 2008 to 1 December 2009 and prior to that he was Shadow Treasurer.\\r\\n\\r\\nIn 2007 he was appointed to Cabinet as the Minister for Environment and Water Resources.\\r\\n\\r\\nElected to Federal Parliament as the Member for Wentworth in 2004, he was appointed Parliamentary Secretary to the Prime Minister with responsibility for national water policy. \\r\\n\\r\\n[Read more on his personal website](http://www.malcolmturnbull.com.au/)\\r\\n\\r\\n### Life and career outside politics\\r\\n\\r\\nMr Turnbull graduated from Sydney University with degrees in Arts and Law. He was a Rhodes scholar and completed a further law degree at Oxford. \\r\\n\\r\\nHe worked as a journalist both in Australia and the United Kingdom before he began legal practice in 1980. He successfully defended the former MI5 agent Peter Wright in his efforts to publish his memoirs, Spycatcher.\\r\\n\\r\\nIn 1987 Mr Turnbull established his own investment banking firm and during that time co-founded a number of Australian companies including OzEmail Ltd – Australia’s first large internet service provider. \\r\\n\\r\\nHe joined Goldman Sachs & Co in 1997 as Chairman of its Australian business, becoming a partner of the global firm in 1998.\\r\\n\\r\\nMalcolm is married to Lucy and they have two adult children.", "short_summary": "Australia’s current Prime Minister is The Hon Malcolm Turnbull MP, Federal Member for Wentworth in New South Wales."}	2016-07-29 03:02:45.858258
221	9	\N	\N	\N	2016-07-26-year-of-achievement-for-children-s-esafety-commissioner	0	2016-07-27 00:51:52.133107	2016-07-27 04:14:55.633918	NewsArticle	{"release_date": "2016-07-26"}	published	9695ea94-7489-43d5-b141-5435b1df5277	\N	\N	{"name": "Year of achievement for Children’s eSafety Commissioner", "options": {}, "summary": "", "content_body": "The Coalition's pledge to protect Australian children from cyber-bullying, online harassment and predatory behaviour has reached an important milestone with the release of a 12-month report card by the Office of the Children's eSafety Commissioner.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe report card found that in its first 12 months of operation the Office has:\\r\\n\\r\\n* Educated more than 59,000 students across Australia through Virtual Classrooms—video presentations delivered online by the Office's eSafety trainers.\\r\\n* Delivered face-to-face presentations to more than 71,000 Australians.\\r\\n* Received 186 serious cyberbullying complaints, most commonly relating to girls (71%) and predominantly involving harmful comments, name-calling and the posting of offensive or upsetting images/videos.\\r\\n* Conducted more than 7,400 investigations into online child sexual abuse content.\\r\\n* Received over 2.9 million page views on its website.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Office was established on 1 July 2015 following a commitment by the Coalition Government to address an issue of major concern for Australian children, parents and schools. Research conducted by the Commonwealth Government found that over a 12-month period, as many as one in five Australian  children  aged eight to seventeen have experienced cyberbullying.\\r\\n\\r\\nFollowing its establishment the Office established an online cyber-bullying complaints system, which has seen the Commissioner work with large social media services to remove harmful cyber-bullying material targeted at Australian children.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Office has also worked closely with students, parents and teachers to teach children how to act responsibly online and to encourage safe, positive online experiences. The Office has developed a wide range of resources to assist educators and parents, and developed advice and education materials  on  how to best respond to cyber-bullying.\\r\\n\\r\\nResources for parents and educators, as well as an online system to report cyber-bullying, illegal or offensive material, are available at [www.esafety.gov.au](https://www.esafety.gov.au).\\r\\n\\r\\n## Media enquiries\\r\\nLuisa Anderson  \\r\\n[0417 309 812](tel:0417309812)  \\r\\n[Luisa.Anderson@communications.gov.au](mailto:Luisa.Anderson@communications.gov.au)", "short_summary": "Release of a 12-month report card by the Office of the Children's eSafety Commissioner."}	2016-07-27 04:14:55.631282
