282	13	\N	\N	\N	2016-07-27-operation-sovereign-borders-no-successful-people-smuggling-boats-in-two-years	0	2016-08-01 02:04:59.109721	2016-08-01 02:05:02.467117	NewsArticle	{"release_date": "2016-07-27"}	published	cec97e62-c308-4fbd-a783-3eaceeea2288	\N	\N	{"name": "Operation Sovereign Borders: no successful people smuggling boats in two years", "options": {}, "content_body": "**Joint media release - [Prime Minister](/prime-minister), Hon. Malcolm Turnbull MP and [Minister for Immigation and Border Protection](/minister-for-immigration-and-border-protection), Hon. Peter Dutton MP**\\r\\n\\r\\nThis achievement is a result of the Coalition's vigilant commitment to its successful border policy.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Prime Minister reiterated his Government's commitment to protecting Australia's borders, stamping out people smuggling and preventing people risking their lives at sea.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\"Secure borders and a well-managed migration system are the bedrock of confidence on which our successful multicultural society is built.\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Minister for Immigration and Border Protection Peter Dutton said Operation Sovereign Borders has been a notable success.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\"Since OSB commenced, 700 people from 28 people smuggling ventures have been returned to their countries of departure,\\" Mr Dutton said.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\"Settlement in Australia will never be an option for people who attempt to travel illegally by boat. There are no exceptions.\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nPeople smugglers should be warned that Australia's maritime assets are strongly positioned to detect and turn back any people smuggling ventures.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\"Intelligence tells us that we must remain resolute because people smugglers are continuing to work hard to convince vulnerable people to get on unsafe people smuggling boats, \\" Mr Dutton said.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\"I urge families here in Australia to tell their loved ones overseas not to risk their lives and waste their money by attempting to come illegally by boat to Australia.\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Government continues its work with regional partners to disrupt people smuggling ventures to prevent vulnerable men, women and children dying at sea.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\"Australia's tough border protection measures remain in place and we are absolutely determined to make sure it stays that way.\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nLabor's abandonment of John Howard's proven border protection policy opened the doors to the people smugglers. The result – 50, 000 unauthorised arrivals on 800 boats, 1,200 deaths at sea, over 8,000 children into detention, 17 detention centres opened and an $11 billion border protection budget blowout.\\r\\n\\r\\nIn contrast, the Coalition has restored security at the border, integrity to our immigration program – and with it the trust of the Australian people. This Government has closed 17 detention centres, removed all the children from detention and increased the humanitarian program from 13,750 to 18,750 by 2018/19.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe are able to increase our annual refugee intake from 13,750 up to 18,750 by 2018/19 because we know we can support those additional numbers and, just as importantly, the community believes we can too.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have been very conscious of the plight of Christians and other persecuted minorities caught in the bitter sectarian conflict in Syria and Iraq. And so we are also welcoming 12,000 refugees from the Syrian conflict zone focused on those persecuted minorities.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe reason Australians welcome high levels of immigration – the highest since the early post-war period – is that we have confidence that our government is in control of our immigration program, deciding who can come here and ensuring that when they do they receive the support needed to integrate into Australian society.\\r\\n\\r\\n##Contact \\r\\nMinister's Office  \\r\\n[02 6277 7860](tel:0262777860)  ", "short_summary": "Today is an important milestone for Operation Sovereign Borders (OSB), marking two years since the last successful people smuggling venture."}	2016-08-01 02:05:02.46395
231	7	\N	\N	\N	2016-07-12-people-s-choice-winner-announced-working-on-country-photography-competition-2016	0	2016-07-27 04:13:11.972222	2016-07-28 23:34:07.247924	NewsArticle	{"release_date": "2016-07-12"}	published	2483fd25-76fe-4422-8357-8004ffdc25b0	\N	\N	{"name": "People's Choice Winner Announced: Working on Country Photography Competition 2016", "options": {}, "summary": "", "content_body": "!['Protecting the Larrakardi' by the Nyikina Mangala Rangers](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AusDTO/gov-au-images/master/Protecting-Larrakardi-Nyikina-Mangala-Rangers.jpg)\\r\\n\\r\\nThis year, the photo 'Protecting the Larrakardi' by the Nyikina Mangala Rangers from the Kimberley in Western Australia has been voted as the most popular photo of the forty shortlisted finalists. \\r\\n\\r\\nThe photograph was taken by Dan Keynes and shows a Nyikina Mangala Ranger protecting a boab tree that's almost one thousand years old. The ranger is using a ‘cool fire’ technique, where annual preventative burning is done just after the wet season, reducing required fuel loads, allowing more effective regeneration and increasing the biodiversity of the Kimberley landscape.\\r\\n\\r\\nOver four thousand people voted for their favourite Working on Country photograph and the winning Nyikina Mangala ranger group will receive a GoPro Hero4 Session camera with headstrap and quickclip as a prize. \\r\\n\\r\\nYou can still view the [forty shortlisted entries](http://www.dpmc.gov.au/indigenous-affairs/environment/photo-competition-2016-vote) for the 2016 Working on Country Photography Competition.", "short_summary": "The winner of the 2016 Working on Country's Photography Competition People's Choice Award has been decided."}	2016-07-28 23:34:07.245686
222	9	\N	\N	\N	2013-11-13-sydney-final-countdown-to-digital-only-tv-has-begun	0	2016-07-27 00:56:02.97928	2016-07-28 23:26:43.093766	NewsArticle	{"release_date": "2013-11-13"}	published	568167b1-b41d-414d-bfbc-f808a66a6c56	\N	\N	{"name": "Sydney — final countdown to digital-only TV has begun!", "options": {}, "summary": "", "content_body": "\\"To watch free-to-air television after this date, you need to be digital ready,\\" Minister for Communications, Malcolm Turnbull said today.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\"The Sydney switchover area includes Gosford, Katoomba and Picton, with over 1.7 million households making the switch. \\r\\n\\r\\n\\"Already, over 94 per cent of households have converted to digital TV since it became available across Sydney in 2001.”\\r\\n\\r\\n\\"If you havent yet switched from analog to digital TV, please dont put it off any longer.\\"\\r\\n\\r\\nMr Turnbull said converting to digital TV involves adding a set-top box or digital recorder to each analog TV or replacing your analog television with a new TV that has a built-in digital tuner.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Household Assistance Scheme is still available to help eligible pensioners who have not yet converted to digital TV. Over 44,000 households across Sydney have been assisted through the Scheme. To check eligibility for this assistance, contact the Department of Human Services on [1800 556 443](tel:1800556443).\\r\\n\\r\\nInformation about the digital switchover and assistance is available on the Digital Ready website at [digitalready.gov.au](https://digitalready.gov.au) or by calling the Digital Ready Information Line on [1800 201 013](tel:1800201013).\\r\\n\\r\\n\\"In December this year, all analog free-to-air television signals will cease and Australian television will be digital-only,\\" Mr Turnbull said. \\r\\n\\r\\n\\"It will be the culmination of work commenced in 2001 which has involved industry, government and the community working in partnership to deliver a better quality television service for Australians.\\"\\r\\n\\r\\n## Media enquiries\\r\\n\\r\\nDigital Switchover  \\r\\nPhone: [02 6271 1777](tel:0262711777)  ", "short_summary": "Sydney and surrounding areas will switch to digital-only TV at 9am on 3 December 2013."}	2016-07-27 03:27:04.726897
