224	8	\N	\N	\N	2016-05-03-2016-australian-government-ict-awards-winners-announced	0	2016-07-27 03:13:32.415426	2016-07-27 04:25:25.908668	NewsArticle	{"release_date": "2016-05-03"}	published	cd46ef10-9638-4b87-8008-d14b4766b509	\N	\N	{"name": "2016 Australian Government ICT Awards - Winners announced!", "options": {}, "summary": "", "content_body": "The Awards showcase the work of government agencies, Federal, State and Local, who are using technology to work smarter and improve the delivery of services within our communities.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Awards also help us to recognise and acknowledge the leadership, dedication and capability of individuals within those agencies in delivering government services.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is the 11th year of the Awards and it was wonderful to see agencies and individuals from around Australia and from all levels of government being nominated for a job well done.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Awards were presented at the CeBIT Australia ICT Gala Dinner and Awards night in Sydney. The [Department of Finance](/department-of-finance) would like to thank Mr John Sheridan, Australian Government Chief Technology Officer for presenting the awards on behalf of the Australian Government.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe details of the winners are listed below:\\r\\n\\r\\n* **Overall Excellence in eGovernment Award & Government 2.0 Category**  \\r\\n **Overall Winner** - MyABDR  \\r\\n National Blood Authority\\r\\n* **Applications Development Category**  \\r\\n**Winner** - Free Trade Agreement Portal  \\r\\nDepartment of Foreign Affairs and Trade\\r\\n* **Geospatial Category**  \\r\\n**Winner** - AgInsight South Australia Information Portal  \\r\\nSouth Australian Department of Primary Industries and Regions\\r\\n* **Government 2.0 Category**  \\r\\n**Winner** - MyABDR  \\r\\nNational Blood Authority\\r\\n* **Project and Program Management**  \\r\\n**Winner** - SV Enabled  \\r\\nSustainability Victoria\\r\\n* **Service Delivery**  \\r\\n**Winner** - iVote at the 2015 NSW State General Election  \\r\\nNew South Wales Electoral Commission\\r\\n* **ICT Young Professional of the Year (under 35 years)**  \\r\\n**Winner** - Chris Moon  \\r\\nSustainability Victoria\\r\\n* **ICT Professional Team of the Year**  \\r\\n**Winner** - Blood Sector Systems Team  \\r\\nNational Blood Authority  \\r\\n\\r\\nCongratulations again to the 2016 Australian government ICT Awards winners.", "short_summary": "It is a great privilege this evening to announce the winners of the 2016 Australian Government ICT Awards."}	2016-07-27 04:25:25.906193
